# Manuscript files (Word-like editor)

The author sees chapters in **Office Viewer** (WYSIWYG). Files on disk are `.md` for backup and AI — she should never need to view raw source.

## Format on disk

- Use standard markdown in files (headings, paragraphs, lists) so the WYSIWYG editor and git backup work correctly.
- One `#` title per chapter file — it renders as the document title in Office Viewer.
- Separate scenes with `##` headings or a horizontal rule (`---`).
- Dialogue in straight double quotes.

## Chapter files

- Naming: `01-chapter-one.md`, `02-the-journey.md` (two-digit prefix, kebab-case slug).
- Always keep `00-table-of-contents.md` in sync when chapters are added, renamed, or reordered.

## Editing style

- Preserve the author’s voice; fix grammar and clarity without flattening personality.
- Prefer small, explainable edits over large rewrites unless asked.
- Flag continuity issues gently (“In chapter 2 you mentioned…”) rather than silently changing facts.
- When explaining formatting to the author, refer to **toolbar buttons** and Word-like shortcuts — not markdown syntax.
